export const PRIVACY_HTML = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Privacy Policy, The Living Bread</title><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://living-bread.org/legal/privacy\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"How The Living Bread collects, uses, shares, keeps and deletes personal data, including through AI assistants.\">\n<style>body{margin:0;background:#F8F5EE;color:#1d2a33;font:16px/1.65 Georgia,serif}main{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 20px 80px}\nh1{font-size:32px;margin:0 0 6px}.u{font:600 12px/1 Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7680}\n.i{font-style:italic;color:#3c4a54}h2{font-size:21px;margin:30px 0 8px}p{margin:0}a{color:#8a6a1f}</style></head>\n<body><main><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><div class=\"u\">The Living Bread \u00b7 Last updated October 5, 2026</div><p class=\"i\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">Your soul is not a data point. We collect as little as we can, we never sell it, and we hold what you share with care. Here is exactly how.</p><h2>What we collect</h2><p>Your account: email address and the name you choose, plus anything you add on purpose: photo, handle, bio, testimony, life verse, spiritual gifts, church, city, state, country, gender, birth year. Location only if you enable it, for the Kingdom map, nearby believers, and Refuge; approximate is enough, and off is allowed. What you create: posts, prayer requests, testimonies, serve offers and needs, bookings, storehouse items and asks, watches, community and church activity, and messages. A push token so notifications can reach this phone, removed when you sign out. The names in Bring Them Home are visible to your account alone.</p><h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use what you give us for these purposes only: to run your account and sign you in; to show your posts, prayers and testimonies to the people you chose; to connect you with believers, churches, gatherings and Tables near you; to deliver the notifications you allowed; to keep the community safe through moderation, reports and abuse prevention; to fix crashes and keep the service working; and, with anonymous totals only, to understand which public pages help people. We never use your prayers, messages or anything you write for advertising, and we never sell or rent any of it.</p><h2>Religious belief is special data</h2><p>Because this is a Christian community, almost everything here reveals religious belief, which many laws, including the GDPR, treat as a special category of personal data. We process it only because you chose to share it, for the purpose you shared it for, and only with the audience you picked. You can withdraw that consent at any time by deleting the content or your account. We never infer your faith, your health or anything sensitive from how you use the app.</p><h2>What we deliberately never keep</h2><p>The Mercy Seat stores nothing you write, not on this phone and not on any server: the words dissolve. The Mirror keeps nothing unless you choose to save it to your own journal. Your streaks, Armor, Crossroads decisions, Family Covenant, and Path to Freedom markers live only on your device. Images and links in private messages are deleted after 24 hours. Angel words arrive without the sender\u2019s identity, and the record pairing angel and receiver is sealed from both.</p><h2>Simon and AI conversations</h2><p>Your conversation history with Simon is stored only on your device, never on our servers. So is anything you ask Simon to remember: those notes stay on your phone, you can see them by asking &quot;What do you remember about me?&quot;, and you can forget any of them, or all of them, at any time. To generate each reply, we send Anthropic, the AI provider: your message and a few recent lines; a short summary of your walk that the app builds on your device (your first name, the season you chose, and your standing prayer need if you set one); open requests you can already see in the app, by first name and city, so Simon can tell you who might need you; and up to three of your remembered notes that relate to your message. Under the API terms we use, that content is not used to train AI models. We do not read, store, or profile your conversations, prayers, or confessions, and nothing you tell Simon is ever used for advertising or recommendations. When you ask Simon to help you share a prayer, it drafts from your own words; nothing is shared until you edit it, choose who sees it, and share it yourself.</p><h2>AI assistants and connectors</h2><p>The Living Bread can be connected to AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Claude and Cursor through our connector server at mcp.living-bread.org. Without signing in, an assistant reads only what is already public: Scripture from our stored text, verses for a need, our public pages, churches, gatherings and communities. If you sign in through the connector, you approve it on a consent screen that names the assistant and what it may read. It can then read, as you, what you could read yourself in the app: the prayers prayed over you, the prayers you gave, your circles, your gatherings and your invitations. The ChatGPT plugin is read only: it cannot post, pray, send, record, delete or change anything. In other assistants you may also allow small acts, such as saying Amen, which happen only when you ask in plain words. What the assistant reads is sent to that assistant&#x27;s provider (for example OpenAI or Anthropic) to answer you, under that provider&#x27;s own privacy policy. We store no conversation from any assistant and never ask an assistant for your chat history. We keep an anonymous log of public questions asked through the connector (the words of the question up to 200 characters, the tool used, the hour, and the name of the assistant), with no account, no IP address and no personal content; it is used only to improve our public pages and is deleted automatically after 90 days. Signed-in reads are not logged. Revoke an assistant at any time in that assistant&#x27;s settings or by signing out of the connector; the server honors the revocation immediately.</p><h2>Who processes data for us</h2><p>Supabase hosts our database, sign-in, and file storage, encrypted in transit and at rest. Anthropic generates Simon\u2019s replies. Expo delivers push notifications and app updates. Mapbox renders maps and answers Refuge searches, receiving the coordinates being searched. AI assistant providers you connect receive only what the assistant reads for you, as described above. Sentry receives crash and performance diagnostics so we can fix problems; these are technical logs, not the content of your prayers or messages. Stripe processes gifts when giving is enabled; we never see your card. Resend sends email such as the welcome note and moderation alerts. Apple or Google handle sign-in when you use their accounts. Each processes data only to provide its service, under its own terms.</p><h2>Fulfillment and shipping addresses</h2><p>When a believer sends you a gift through Kingdom Fulfillment, you may share where to send it: a name, an address, and an optional phone number. This is used for one thing, to deliver the gift, and is shared only with the small designated fulfillment team who purchases and ships it. It is never shown to the giver, who sees only that a gift is on the way. Addresses are stored encrypted, kept no longer than the delivery needs, and you can ask us to remove yours at any time. Payment for a gift, when charged, is handled by Stripe; we never see your card.</p><h2>What we will never do</h2><p>We will never sell your information. The app itself shows you no advertising and runs no third-party analytics or advertising technology inside it. Our public website may use standard, privacy-respecting analytics to understand how pages are found and read; it is never joined to your account, and we never track you across other companies\u2019 apps or websites, so there is no App Tracking Transparency prompt to answer. We will never use your prayers, confessions, temptations, or struggles to target, rank, or advertise to you. Your weakness is not our merchandise.</p><h2>How long we keep things</h2><p>Your account and everything you create remain until you delete them; you can edit or delete any of your content at any time. Images and links in private messages are deleted after 24 hours. The anonymous connector question log is deleted after 90 days. Crash diagnostics are kept by Sentry for up to 90 days. Fulfillment addresses are kept only until the gift is delivered. Deleting your account removes everything by cascade, including your photos and voice recordings in storage, within 30 days from backups, and cannot be undone. Reports and moderation records needed to keep the community safe may be kept for up to one year after an account is deleted, without your content.</p><h2>Your controls</h2><p>Delete your account and all of its data any time in Settings under Account, or on the web at living-bread.org/delete-account; deletion is permanent and removes everything by cascade. Control location, visibility, and notifications in Settings and your profile. Block anyone instantly, they disappear from your feed and can no longer message you; report anything with one tap and it reaches our moderation team. To request a copy of your data or ask a privacy question, email support@living-bread.org.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>The Living Bread is for people 13 and older. Kids and youth rooms are written for families to walk together under a parent\u2019s account. We do not knowingly collect accounts from children under 13; tell us and we will remove one.</p><h2>Sensitive things, named plainly</h2><p>Prayer, confession, health, addiction, and family are among the most sensitive things a person can share. We minimize what is stored, restrict internal access, and will notify affected people and authorities as the law requires if a breach ever occurs. Please know: conversations in this app, including with Simon, are not legally privileged the way conversations with clergy, a therapist, or a lawyer may be.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we will say so in the app before it takes effect. Questions, requests, or privacy concerns: email support@living-bread.org, or visit living-bread.org/support.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:34px\">Publisher: The Living Bread, 1414 12th Ave, Seattle, Washington, United States. Contact: <a href=\"mailto:support@living-bread.org\">support@living-bread.org</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://living-bread.org/support\">living-bread.org/support</a></p></main></body></html>";
